{"post_stream":{"posts":[{"id":278053,"name":"Petr Viktorin","username":"encukou","avatar_template":"/user_avatar/discuss.python.org/encukou/{size}/2461_2.png","created_at":"2025-11-21T14:43:52.643Z","cooked":"\u003cp\u003eHi!\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eI’d like to expand the \u003ca href=\"https://peps.python.org/pep-0011/#all-other-platforms\"\u003eAll other platforms\u003c/a\u003e section of PEP 11 (CPython platform support), to make it clear that we support and encourage efforts to bring Python to places where the core team can’t reach – but we can’t be responsible if things break there, and we can clean up cruft.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eI’d also like to add a section on POSIX platforms.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThe initial proposal text is below; I also have a \u003ca href=\"https://github.com/encukou/peps/pull/3/files\"\u003epull request\u003c/a\u003e that might get updates.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eWhat do you think?\u003cbr\u003e\ncc \u003ca class=\"mention\" href=\"/u/brettcannon\"\u003e@brettcannon\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003chr\u003e\n\u003ch2\u003e\u003ca name=\"p-278053-rationale-1\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-278053-rationale-1\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003eRationale\u003c/h2\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e[The small text is substantially unchanged]\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e\u003csmall\u003eOver time, the CPython source code has collected various pieces of platform-specific code, which, at some point in time, was considered necessary to use CPython on a specific platform. Without access to this platform, it is not possible to determine whether this code is still needed. As a result, this code may either break during CPython’s evolution, or it may become unnecessary as the platforms evolve as well.\u003c/small\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003csmall\u003e\n\u003c/small\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003csmall\u003eAllowing these fragments to grow poses the risk of unmaintainability: without having experts for a large number of platforms, it is not possible to determine whether a certain change to the CPython source code will work on all supported platforms. To reduce this risk, this PEP specifies what is required for a platform to be considered supported\u003c/small\u003e by the CPython core team, as well as providing a procedure to remove code for platforms with few or no CPython users.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eOn the other hand, allowing these fragments in the main repository can promote collaboration, can help identify non-portable parts of the code base, and is necessary for bootstrapping support for a “new” platform. This PEP specifies what it means for a platform to be “unsupported”, and how the core team handles code for such platforms.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThis PEP also explicitly lists what platforms are directly \u003cem\u003esupported\u003c/em\u003e by the CPython development team.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch3\u003e\u003ca name=\"p-278053-h-2\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-278053-h-2\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003e[…]\u003c/h3\u003e\n\u003ch2\u003e\u003ca name=\"p-278053-unsupported-platforms-instead-of-all-other-platforms-3\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-278053-unsupported-platforms-instead-of-all-other-platforms-3\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003eUnsupported platforms [instead of “All other platforms”]\u003c/h2\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eAll platforms not listed in the above tiers are \u003cem\u003eunsupported\u003c/em\u003e by the core team. The core team does not develop and test on such platforms, and so they cannot provide any promises that Python will work on them.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eHowever, the code base does include unsupported code – that is, code specific to unsupported platforms. Contributions in this area are welcome as long as they:\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cul\u003e\n\u003cli\u003epose a minimal maintenance burden to the core team, and\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003ebenefit substantially more people than the contributor.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003c/ul\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eWe assume contributors are able to maintain modifications/patches, test patched builds, redistribute modified code, make promises to their users, and otherwise support “their” platform. With that in mind, it is generally unnecessary to backport unsupported fixes to CPython’s maintenance branches.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eUnsupported code that \u003cem\u003edoes\u003c/em\u003e cause a maintenance burden, or obstructs general improvements, may be rejected or removed from the code base without a deprecation process. Core team members that do this intentionally are expected to seek out and notify interested parties, to review any submitted fixes (if inobtrusive), and to consider adding configuration or extension capabilities necessary for workarounds.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003ePeople interested in unsupported platforms may add themselves to the \u003ca href=\"https://devguide.python.org/core-team/experts/#platforms\"\u003ePlatforms experts list\u003c/a\u003e in the Cpython contributor’s guide to request that they be notified on issues related to “their” platform. There is, however, no formal guarantee that they \u003cem\u003ewill\u003c/em\u003e be notified.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e\u003csmall\u003ePlatforms not listed in this PEP may also be supported by the wider Python community in other ways. If your desired platform is not listed above, please perform a search online to see if someone is already providing support in some form.\u003c/small\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch2\u003e\u003ca name=\"p-278053-h-4\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-278053-h-4\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003e[…]\u003c/h2\u003e\n\u003ch3\u003e\u003ca name=\"p-278053-posix-after-windows-5\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-278053-posix-after-windows-5\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003ePOSIX [after “Windows”]\u003c/h3\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eFeatures specified in POSIX are expected to work according to the standard. This cuts two ways:\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cul\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eIf a POSIX feature is available, it is expected to conform to POSIX.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eWorkarounds for out-of-spec platforms are acceptable. For unsupported platforms, disabling functionality is preferred over a non-trivial workaround.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eCPython should make no assumptions about these features beyond what’s specified in POSIX.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eFor example, while POSIX specifies errno as an int with no restrictions, error codes on all supported platforms happen to be positive. Relying on this would be considered a bug, even if it only manifests on unsupported platforms.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003c/ul\u003e","post_number":1,"post_type":1,"posts_count":12,"updated_at":"2025-11-21T14:43:52.643Z","reply_count":2,"reply_to_post_number":null,"quote_count":0,"incoming_link_count":299,"reads":157,"readers_count":156,"score":1641.4,"yours":false,"topic_id":104986,"topic_slug":"proposed-pep-11-update-policy-for-unsupported-platforms","display_username":"Petr Viktorin","primary_group_name":"committers","flair_name":null,"flair_url":null,"flair_bg_color":null,"flair_color":null,"flair_group_id":null,"badges_granted":[],"version":1,"can_edit":false,"can_delete":false,"can_recover":false,"can_see_hidden_post":false,"can_wiki":false,"link_counts":[{"url":"https://github.com/encukou/peps/pull/3/files","internal":false,"reflection":false,"title":"PEP 11: Unsupported platforms \u0026 POSIX by encukou · Pull Request #3 · encukou/peps · GitHub","clicks":12},{"url":"https://peps.python.org/pep-0011/#all-other-platforms","internal":false,"reflection":false,"title":"PEP 11 – CPython platform support | peps.python.org","clicks":12},{"url":"https://devguide.python.org/core-team/experts/#platforms","internal":false,"reflection":false,"title":"Experts index","clicks":2},{"url":"https://discuss.python.org/t/macos-version-support-policy/53715/20","internal":true,"reflection":true,"title":"macOS version support policy","clicks":1}],"read":true,"user_title":"CPython core developer","title_is_group":true,"bookmarked":false,"actions_summary":[{"id":2,"count":8}],"moderator":true,"admin":true,"staff":true,"user_id":26,"hidden":false,"trust_level":3,"deleted_at":null,"user_deleted":false,"edit_reason":null,"can_view_edit_history":true,"wiki":false,"post_url":"/t/proposed-pep-11-update-policy-for-unsupported-platforms/104986/1","reactions":[{"id":"heart","type":"emoji","count":8}],"current_user_reaction":null,"reaction_users_count":8,"current_user_used_main_reaction":false,"can_accept_answer":false,"can_unaccept_answer":false,"accepted_answer":false,"topic_accepted_answer":null,"can_vote":false},{"id":278114,"name":"H. Vetinari","username":"h-vetinari","avatar_template":"/user_avatar/discuss.python.org/h-vetinari/{size}/1220_2.png","created_at":"2025-11-22T06:04:07.080Z","cooked":"\u003cp\u003eIf we’re updating PEP 11, I feel we should add lower bounds also for the versions of the supported platforms. For example minimum versions for glibc, macOS (c.f. this \u003ca href=\"https://discuss.python.org/t/macos-version-support-policy/53715\"\u003ediscussion\u003c/a\u003e) or windows, which probably closely correspond to whatever’s being tested in CI regularly.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eFor example, I doubt that anyone would consider CentOS 6 with glibc 2.12 from 2010 (EOL in 2020) still supported. Windows \u0026lt;10 (or \u0026lt;7 or \u0026lt;8) might also be bitrotting fast. That sort of thing\u003c/p\u003e","post_number":2,"post_type":1,"posts_count":12,"updated_at":"2025-11-22T06:04:07.080Z","reply_count":2,"reply_to_post_number":null,"quote_count":0,"incoming_link_count":2,"reads":125,"readers_count":124,"score":90.0,"yours":false,"topic_id":104986,"topic_slug":"proposed-pep-11-update-policy-for-unsupported-platforms","display_username":"H. Vetinari","primary_group_name":null,"flair_name":null,"flair_url":null,"flair_bg_color":null,"flair_color":null,"flair_group_id":null,"badges_granted":[],"version":1,"can_edit":false,"can_delete":false,"can_recover":false,"can_see_hidden_post":false,"can_wiki":false,"link_counts":[{"url":"https://discuss.python.org/t/macos-version-support-policy/53715","internal":true,"reflection":false,"title":"macOS version support policy","clicks":4}],"read":true,"user_title":null,"bookmarked":false,"actions_summary":[{"id":2,"count":3}],"moderator":false,"admin":false,"staff":false,"user_id":1017,"hidden":false,"trust_level":2,"deleted_at":null,"user_deleted":false,"edit_reason":null,"can_view_edit_history":true,"wiki":false,"post_url":"/t/proposed-pep-11-update-policy-for-unsupported-platforms/104986/2","reactions":[{"id":"heart","type":"emoji","count":3}],"current_user_reaction":null,"reaction_users_count":3,"current_user_used_main_reaction":false,"can_accept_answer":false,"can_unaccept_answer":false,"accepted_answer":false,"topic_accepted_answer":null},{"id":278120,"name":"Chris Angelico","username":"Rosuav","avatar_template":"/user_avatar/discuss.python.org/rosuav/{size}/3429_2.png","created_at":"2025-11-22T07:33:58.138Z","cooked":"\u003caside class=\"quote no-group\" data-username=\"h-vetinari\" data-post=\"2\" data-topic=\"104986\"\u003e\n\u003cdiv class=\"title\"\u003e\n\u003cdiv class=\"quote-controls\"\u003e\u003c/div\u003e\n\u003cimg alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://sea2.discourse-cdn.com/flex002/user_avatar/discuss.python.org/h-vetinari/48/1220_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"\u003e H. Vetinari:\u003c/div\u003e\n\u003cblockquote\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eWindows \u0026lt;10 (or \u0026lt;7 or \u0026lt;8) might also be bitrotting fast.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003c/blockquote\u003e\n\u003c/aside\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eWindows support levels are already specified in PEP 11 (tied to Microsoft’s support - basically, if MS drops support, Python can drop support as of the next release).\u003c/p\u003e","post_number":3,"post_type":1,"posts_count":12,"updated_at":"2025-11-22T07:33:58.138Z","reply_count":0,"reply_to_post_number":2,"quote_count":1,"incoming_link_count":1,"reads":123,"readers_count":122,"score":59.6,"yours":false,"topic_id":104986,"topic_slug":"proposed-pep-11-update-policy-for-unsupported-platforms","display_username":"Chris Angelico","primary_group_name":null,"flair_name":null,"flair_url":null,"flair_bg_color":null,"flair_color":null,"flair_group_id":null,"badges_granted":[],"version":1,"can_edit":false,"can_delete":false,"can_recover":false,"can_see_hidden_post":false,"can_wiki":false,"read":true,"user_title":null,"bookmarked":false,"actions_summary":[{"id":2,"count":2}],"moderator":false,"admin":false,"staff":false,"user_id":3377,"hidden":false,"trust_level":3,"deleted_at":null,"user_deleted":false,"edit_reason":null,"can_view_edit_history":true,"wiki":false,"post_url":"/t/proposed-pep-11-update-policy-for-unsupported-platforms/104986/3","reactions":[{"id":"heart","type":"emoji","count":2}],"current_user_reaction":null,"reaction_users_count":2,"current_user_used_main_reaction":false,"can_accept_answer":false,"can_unaccept_answer":false,"accepted_answer":false,"topic_accepted_answer":null},{"id":278122,"name":"Hugo van Kemenade","username":"hugovk","avatar_template":"/user_avatar/discuss.python.org/hugovk/{size}/14505_2.png","created_at":"2025-11-22T07:53:55.109Z","cooked":"\u003caside class=\"quote no-group\" data-username=\"h-vetinari\" data-post=\"2\" data-topic=\"104986\"\u003e\n\u003cdiv class=\"title\"\u003e\n\u003cdiv class=\"quote-controls\"\u003e\u003c/div\u003e\n\u003cimg alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://sea2.discourse-cdn.com/flex002/user_avatar/discuss.python.org/h-vetinari/48/1220_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"\u003e H. Vetinari:\u003c/div\u003e\n\u003cblockquote\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eIf we’re updating PEP 11, I feel we should add lower bounds also for the versions of the supported platforms.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003c/blockquote\u003e\n\u003c/aside\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eI suggest opening a new topic.\u003c/p\u003e","post_number":4,"post_type":1,"posts_count":12,"updated_at":"2025-11-22T07:53:55.109Z","reply_count":1,"reply_to_post_number":2,"quote_count":1,"incoming_link_count":2,"reads":122,"readers_count":121,"score":99.4,"yours":false,"topic_id":104986,"topic_slug":"proposed-pep-11-update-policy-for-unsupported-platforms","display_username":"Hugo van Kemenade","primary_group_name":"committers","flair_name":"committers","flair_url":"https://us1.discourse-cdn.com/flex002/uploads/python1/original/1X/ca0883b21b8210c5a62c9ac02353de5f24a4d6fc.png","flair_bg_color":"006b94","flair_color":"fac731","flair_group_id":41,"badges_granted":[],"version":1,"can_edit":false,"can_delete":false,"can_recover":false,"can_see_hidden_post":false,"can_wiki":false,"read":true,"user_title":"CPython core developer","title_is_group":true,"bookmarked":false,"actions_summary":[{"id":2,"count":4}],"moderator":false,"admin":false,"staff":false,"user_id":358,"hidden":false,"trust_level":3,"deleted_at":null,"user_deleted":false,"edit_reason":null,"can_view_edit_history":true,"wiki":false,"post_url":"/t/proposed-pep-11-update-policy-for-unsupported-platforms/104986/4","reactions":[{"id":"heart","type":"emoji","count":4}],"current_user_reaction":null,"reaction_users_count":4,"current_user_used_main_reaction":false,"can_accept_answer":false,"can_unaccept_answer":false,"accepted_answer":false,"topic_accepted_answer":null},{"id":278169,"name":"H. Vetinari","username":"h-vetinari","avatar_template":"/user_avatar/discuss.python.org/h-vetinari/{size}/1220_2.png","created_at":"2025-11-22T21:35:51.011Z","cooked":"\u003caside class=\"quote group-committers\" data-username=\"hugovk\" data-post=\"4\" data-topic=\"104986\"\u003e\n\u003cdiv class=\"title\"\u003e\n\u003cdiv class=\"quote-controls\"\u003e\u003c/div\u003e\n\u003cimg alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://sea2.discourse-cdn.com/flex002/user_avatar/discuss.python.org/hugovk/48/14505_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"\u003e Hugo van Kemenade:\u003c/div\u003e\n\u003cblockquote\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eI suggest opening a new topic.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003c/blockquote\u003e\n\u003c/aside\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eWhy? “policy for unsupported platforms” is \u003cem\u003eexactly\u003c/em\u003e the topic I’m talking about.\u003c/p\u003e","post_number":5,"post_type":1,"posts_count":12,"updated_at":"2025-11-22T21:35:51.011Z","reply_count":1,"reply_to_post_number":4,"quote_count":1,"incoming_link_count":2,"reads":111,"readers_count":110,"score":52.2,"yours":false,"topic_id":104986,"topic_slug":"proposed-pep-11-update-policy-for-unsupported-platforms","display_username":"H. Vetinari","primary_group_name":null,"flair_name":null,"flair_url":null,"flair_bg_color":null,"flair_color":null,"flair_group_id":null,"badges_granted":[],"version":1,"can_edit":false,"can_delete":false,"can_recover":false,"can_see_hidden_post":false,"can_wiki":false,"read":true,"user_title":null,"bookmarked":false,"actions_summary":[{"id":2,"count":1}],"moderator":false,"admin":false,"staff":false,"user_id":1017,"hidden":false,"trust_level":2,"deleted_at":null,"user_deleted":false,"edit_reason":null,"can_view_edit_history":true,"wiki":false,"post_url":"/t/proposed-pep-11-update-policy-for-unsupported-platforms/104986/5","reactions":[{"id":"heart","type":"emoji","count":1}],"current_user_reaction":null,"reaction_users_count":1,"current_user_used_main_reaction":false,"can_accept_answer":false,"can_unaccept_answer":false,"accepted_answer":false,"topic_accepted_answer":null},{"id":278173,"name":"Gregory P. Smith","username":"gpshead","avatar_template":"/user_avatar/discuss.python.org/gpshead/{size}/54_2.png","created_at":"2025-11-22T23:05:03.657Z","cooked":"\u003cp\u003eAdding lower bounds is a \u003cem\u003eseparate\u003c/em\u003e discussion and decision than the specific edits that Petr wanted to focus on in this thread. Additional requests can derail a discussion and resolution by going in too many directions at once.\u003c/p\u003e","post_number":6,"post_type":1,"posts_count":12,"updated_at":"2025-11-22T23:05:03.657Z","reply_count":0,"reply_to_post_number":5,"quote_count":0,"incoming_link_count":2,"reads":107,"readers_count":106,"score":166.4,"yours":false,"topic_id":104986,"topic_slug":"proposed-pep-11-update-policy-for-unsupported-platforms","display_username":"Gregory P. Smith","primary_group_name":"committers","flair_name":"committers","flair_url":"https://us1.discourse-cdn.com/flex002/uploads/python1/original/1X/ca0883b21b8210c5a62c9ac02353de5f24a4d6fc.png","flair_bg_color":"006b94","flair_color":"fac731","flair_group_id":41,"badges_granted":[],"version":1,"can_edit":false,"can_delete":false,"can_recover":false,"can_see_hidden_post":false,"can_wiki":false,"read":true,"user_title":"CPython core developer","title_is_group":true,"reply_to_user":{"id":1017,"username":"h-vetinari","name":"H. Vetinari","avatar_template":"/user_avatar/discuss.python.org/h-vetinari/{size}/1220_2.png"},"bookmarked":false,"actions_summary":[{"id":2,"count":7}],"moderator":false,"admin":false,"staff":false,"user_id":51,"hidden":false,"trust_level":3,"deleted_at":null,"user_deleted":false,"edit_reason":null,"can_view_edit_history":true,"wiki":false,"post_url":"/t/proposed-pep-11-update-policy-for-unsupported-platforms/104986/6","reactions":[{"id":"heart","type":"emoji","count":7}],"current_user_reaction":null,"reaction_users_count":7,"current_user_used_main_reaction":false,"can_accept_answer":false,"can_unaccept_answer":false,"accepted_answer":false,"topic_accepted_answer":null},{"id":278174,"name":"Gregory P. Smith","username":"gpshead","avatar_template":"/user_avatar/discuss.python.org/gpshead/{size}/54_2.png","created_at":"2025-11-22T23:11:17.013Z","cooked":"\u003caside class=\"quote group-committers\" data-username=\"encukou\" data-post=\"1\" data-topic=\"104986\"\u003e\n\u003cdiv class=\"title\"\u003e\n\u003cdiv class=\"quote-controls\"\u003e\u003c/div\u003e\n\u003cimg alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://sea2.discourse-cdn.com/flex002/user_avatar/discuss.python.org/encukou/48/2461_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"\u003e encukou:\u003c/div\u003e\n\u003cblockquote\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eCore team members that do this intentionally are expected to seek out and notify interested parties, to review any submitted fixes (if inobtrusive), and to consider adding configuration or extension capabilities necessary for workarounds.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003ePeople interested in unsupported platforms may add themselves to the \u003ca href=\"https://devguide.python.org/core-team/experts/#platforms\"\u003ePlatforms experts list\u003c/a\u003e in the Cpython contributor’s guide to request that they be notified on issues related to “their” platform. There is, however, no formal guarantee that they \u003cem\u003ewill\u003c/em\u003e be notified.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003c/blockquote\u003e\n\u003c/aside\u003e\n\u003cp\u003ethe wording here could probably be tightened up a bit.  I like that you chose to say “notify” as that is really all we should try to do.  That is good because we should never allow unsupported things to block our work.  but saying “expected to” is perhaps a bit strong when the next paragraph is more realistic about there being no formal guarantees about notification.  I’d change “expected to” to “are encouraged to” and directly include mention of the platforms experts list there as that is the \u003cem\u003ehow\u003c/em\u003e part of what we want to encourage people to do.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e\u003cem\u003e(additional context: Petr joined the steering council for office hours this week, part of our discussion was related to this topic)\u003c/em\u003e\u003c/p\u003e","post_number":7,"post_type":1,"posts_count":12,"updated_at":"2025-11-22T23:11:17.013Z","reply_count":1,"reply_to_post_number":null,"quote_count":1,"incoming_link_count":2,"reads":106,"readers_count":105,"score":96.2,"yours":false,"topic_id":104986,"topic_slug":"proposed-pep-11-update-policy-for-unsupported-platforms","display_username":"Gregory P. Smith","primary_group_name":"committers","flair_name":"committers","flair_url":"https://us1.discourse-cdn.com/flex002/uploads/python1/original/1X/ca0883b21b8210c5a62c9ac02353de5f24a4d6fc.png","flair_bg_color":"006b94","flair_color":"fac731","flair_group_id":41,"badges_granted":[],"version":1,"can_edit":false,"can_delete":false,"can_recover":false,"can_see_hidden_post":false,"can_wiki":false,"read":true,"user_title":"CPython core developer","title_is_group":true,"bookmarked":false,"actions_summary":[{"id":2,"count":2}],"moderator":false,"admin":false,"staff":false,"user_id":51,"hidden":false,"trust_level":3,"deleted_at":null,"user_deleted":false,"edit_reason":null,"can_view_edit_history":true,"wiki":false,"post_url":"/t/proposed-pep-11-update-policy-for-unsupported-platforms/104986/7","reactions":[{"id":"heart","type":"emoji","count":2}],"current_user_reaction":null,"reaction_users_count":2,"current_user_used_main_reaction":false,"can_accept_answer":false,"can_unaccept_answer":false,"accepted_answer":false,"topic_accepted_answer":null},{"id":278380,"name":"Petr Viktorin","username":"encukou","avatar_template":"/user_avatar/discuss.python.org/encukou/{size}/2461_2.png","created_at":"2025-11-25T15:50:36.340Z","cooked":"\u003cp\u003eThanks! I’ve \u003ca href=\"https://github.com/encukou/peps/pull/3/commits/bbd33a53c27396f6b6fbcb215b154b09386f0a18\"\u003eupdated the PR\u003c/a\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003caside class=\"quote group-committers\" data-username=\"gpshead\" data-post=\"7\" data-topic=\"104986\"\u003e\n\u003cdiv class=\"title\"\u003e\n\u003cdiv class=\"quote-controls\"\u003e\u003c/div\u003e\n\u003cimg alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://sea2.discourse-cdn.com/flex002/user_avatar/discuss.python.org/gpshead/48/54_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"\u003e Gregory P. Smith:\u003c/div\u003e\n\u003cblockquote\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e(additional context: Petr joined the steering council for office hours this week, part of our discussion was related to this topic)\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003c/blockquote\u003e\n\u003c/aside\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThat, and I’ve looked at \u003ccode\u003eOS-unsupported\u003c/code\u003e issues in the past months, thinking about out how I’d like them handled in general :‍)\u003c/p\u003e","post_number":8,"post_type":1,"posts_count":12,"updated_at":"2025-11-25T15:50:36.340Z","reply_count":0,"reply_to_post_number":7,"quote_count":1,"incoming_link_count":1,"reads":95,"readers_count":94,"score":39.0,"yours":false,"topic_id":104986,"topic_slug":"proposed-pep-11-update-policy-for-unsupported-platforms","display_username":"Petr Viktorin","primary_group_name":"committers","flair_name":null,"flair_url":null,"flair_bg_color":null,"flair_color":null,"flair_group_id":null,"badges_granted":[],"version":1,"can_edit":false,"can_delete":false,"can_recover":false,"can_see_hidden_post":false,"can_wiki":false,"link_counts":[{"url":"https://github.com/encukou/peps/pull/3/commits/bbd33a53c27396f6b6fbcb215b154b09386f0a18","internal":false,"reflection":false,"title":"PEP 11: Unsupported platforms \u0026 POSIX by encukou · Pull Request #3 · encukou/peps · GitHub","clicks":3}],"read":true,"user_title":"CPython core developer","title_is_group":true,"bookmarked":false,"actions_summary":[{"id":2,"count":1}],"moderator":true,"admin":true,"staff":true,"user_id":26,"hidden":false,"trust_level":3,"deleted_at":null,"user_deleted":false,"edit_reason":null,"can_view_edit_history":true,"wiki":false,"post_url":"/t/proposed-pep-11-update-policy-for-unsupported-platforms/104986/8","reactions":[{"id":"heart","type":"emoji","count":1}],"current_user_reaction":null,"reaction_users_count":1,"current_user_used_main_reaction":false,"can_accept_answer":false,"can_unaccept_answer":false,"accepted_answer":false,"topic_accepted_answer":null},{"id":278435,"name":"Brett Cannon","username":"brettcannon","avatar_template":"/user_avatar/discuss.python.org/brettcannon/{size}/34895_2.png","created_at":"2025-11-25T23:24:17.927Z","cooked":"\u003caside class=\"quote group-committers\" data-username=\"encukou\" data-post=\"1\" data-topic=\"104986\"\u003e\n\u003cdiv class=\"title\"\u003e\n\u003cdiv class=\"quote-controls\"\u003e\u003c/div\u003e\n\u003cimg alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://sea2.discourse-cdn.com/flex002/user_avatar/discuss.python.org/encukou/48/2461_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"\u003e Petr Viktorin:\u003c/div\u003e\n\u003cblockquote\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eWhat do you think?\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003c/blockquote\u003e\n\u003c/aside\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eI think it’s reasonable. To summarize my interpretation, we are saying we have code for unsupported platforms and that’s OK, but it doesn’t imply any promises either.\u003c/p\u003e","post_number":9,"post_type":1,"posts_count":12,"updated_at":"2025-11-25T23:24:17.927Z","reply_count":1,"reply_to_post_number":null,"quote_count":1,"incoming_link_count":2,"reads":91,"readers_count":90,"score":48.2,"yours":false,"topic_id":104986,"topic_slug":"proposed-pep-11-update-policy-for-unsupported-platforms","display_username":"Brett Cannon","primary_group_name":"committers","flair_name":"packaging-council","flair_url":"https://us1.discourse-cdn.com/flex002/uploads/python1/original/3X/0/5/05b580b0d5d0ba0258ddcb3685ca7006fcd0f01b.png","flair_bg_color":"","flair_color":"","flair_group_id":48,"badges_granted":[],"version":1,"can_edit":false,"can_delete":false,"can_recover":false,"can_see_hidden_post":false,"can_wiki":false,"read":true,"user_title":"Packaging Council Member","title_is_group":false,"bookmarked":false,"actions_summary":[{"id":2,"count":1}],"moderator":true,"admin":true,"staff":true,"user_id":36,"hidden":false,"trust_level":4,"deleted_at":null,"user_deleted":false,"edit_reason":null,"can_view_edit_history":true,"wiki":false,"post_url":"/t/proposed-pep-11-update-policy-for-unsupported-platforms/104986/9","reactions":[{"id":"heart","type":"emoji","count":1}],"current_user_reaction":null,"reaction_users_count":1,"current_user_used_main_reaction":false,"can_accept_answer":false,"can_unaccept_answer":false,"accepted_answer":false,"topic_accepted_answer":null},{"id":278468,"name":"Petr Viktorin","username":"encukou","avatar_template":"/user_avatar/discuss.python.org/encukou/{size}/2461_2.png","created_at":"2025-11-26T09:32:36.773Z","cooked":"\u003caside class=\"quote group-committers\" data-username=\"brettcannon\" data-display-name=\"Brett Cannon\" data-post=\"9\" data-topic=\"104986\"\u003e\n\u003cdiv class=\"title\"\u003e\n\u003cdiv class=\"quote-controls\"\u003e\u003c/div\u003e\n\u003cimg alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://sea2.discourse-cdn.com/flex002/user_avatar/discuss.python.org/brettcannon/48/34895_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"\u003e Brett Cannon:\u003c/div\u003e\n\u003cblockquote\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eTo summarize my interpretation, we are saying we have code for unsupported platforms and that’s OK, but it doesn’t imply any promises either.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003c/blockquote\u003e\n\u003c/aside\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eA good summary, focused at the bits in the repo.\u003cbr\u003e\nI’d add that we welcome and encourage people that support CPython on other platforms – without promising any particular level of welcoming and encouragement.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e(Which is especially important ­now that we might need to clarify that the difference between a supported and non-supported platform can be as much as \u003ca href=\"https://discuss.python.org/t/python-3-14-0-is-incompatible-with-stack-switching-systems-what-do-we-do/104880\"\u003eusing a multitasking library\u003c/a\u003e…)\u003c/p\u003e","post_number":10,"post_type":1,"posts_count":12,"updated_at":"2025-11-26T09:32:36.773Z","reply_count":0,"reply_to_post_number":9,"quote_count":1,"incoming_link_count":12,"reads":94,"readers_count":93,"score":138.8,"yours":false,"topic_id":104986,"topic_slug":"proposed-pep-11-update-policy-for-unsupported-platforms","display_username":"Petr Viktorin","primary_group_name":"committers","flair_name":null,"flair_url":null,"flair_b